{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"congenial-cibophobic-goosefish","creation_channel":"mcp","description":"## Context / Problem\nThe scripts cohort contains audited comments or docstrings that obscure current behavior with repetition, obvious narration, duplicated explanation, or historical detail. The audit is pinned to `9e65567b79ffe872534c3c656ade7b34340d8192`.\n\n## Approach\nEdit explanatory text only in this directory/subsystem cohort. Condense it to current, non-obvious rationale and constraints; retain every file-specific preserve item and consumer contract below. Grouping adjacent files from one subsystem keeps the change reviewable in one session and permits one coherent verification pass without changing executable behavior.\n\n## Scope\n- `scripts/check_import_walk.py:1–37, 77–79` — Preserve package/script isolation semantics and explicit skip policy. Consumer: argparse consumes only the first docstring line.\n- `scripts/check_mcp_library_parity.py:2–59, 156–171, 291–321` — Preserve descriptors, correspondence, normalization, divergence reasons, stand-in recovery, manifest coherence. Consumer: argparse consumes only the first line.\n- `scripts/check_mechanism_delta.py:2–58` — Preserve seven kinds/partition, marker contract, ratchet and exit semantics, portability. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_orphaned_load.py:2–61, 75–91` — Preserve PPID+CPU signal, system exclusions, read-only triage, threshold/path basis. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/check_raw_git_writes.py:2–104` — Preserve Layer P/W/R3 semantics, sanctions, trust boundary, accepted residuals. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_repo_root_from_package.py:2–39` — Preserve wheel-install invariant, exact composing shape, sanction versus seam. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_repo_root_from_tracker.py:2–59, 83–88` — Preserve store invariant, wrapper shapes, sanction/seam distinction. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_server_manifest.py:2–26` — Preserve code/manifest parity and canonical optional fields. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/check_shellcheck.py:2–25` — Preserve warning severity required for SC2115, scope, missing binary fails. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_ssm_secret_state.py:2–45` — Preserve plaintext-state threat, exact violations, generated-expression exception, hermetic/no-secret-output contract. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_templatefile_escapes.py:2–28` — Preserve comments remain template text, declared-root rule, why ShellCheck cannot detect it. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_tickets_boundary.py:2–38` — Preserve relocatable store, four shapes, reasoned marker, legitimate exceptions. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/check_uv_pin.py:2–38` — Preserve exact single source, defeat modes, uv tag/digest agreement, portability. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/check_verify_gate_parity.py:2–27` — Preserve Verified superset rule, source-lane scope, justified exclusions. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/dependency_audit.py:2–37, 51–54, 191–199` — Preserve lane-aware verdicts, severity fallback, sibling-import requirement, call-time sleep seam. Consumer: full argparse `--help`.\n- `scripts/gen_env_registry.py:2–56, 72–109, 112–132, 151–173` — Preserve supported patterns, unknown-accessor/helper/stale-row failures, exclusions, update usage. Consumer: none found.\n- `scripts/install-gerrit-hook.sh:2–24` — Preserve common-dir/worktree safety, non-clobbering, idempotency, usage/env overrides. Consumer: manual source readers.\n- `scripts/jira_dc_capability_map.py:2–34, 52–57, 102–114, 549–577, 702–705, 721–724` — Preserve authoring-tool constraints, evidence capture, fail-soft digest, custom-field discriminator, artifact verification. Consumer: module docstring is argparse `--help`; L215–232 is an LLM tool contract and was intentionally not flagged.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Every listed location contains only current, non-obvious rationale or constraints after remediation; verified by reviewing the final diff against every Scope row.\n- [ ] Every preserve item and consumer contract in Scope remains explicit and accurate; verified by a row-by-row completion comment and the commands under Verification.\n- [ ] No executable behavior or test assertion changes; verified by the commands under Verification exiting 0.\n\n## Verification\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" make lint`\n- `env PATH=\"$PWD/.venv/bin:$PATH\" .venv/bin/python scripts/check_comment_hygiene.py`\n\nThe row-by-row diff review is authoritative for prose quality; the hygiene guard detects only its narrow deterministic history-token rule.","id":"5f00-e694-dab6-4d1c","parent_id":"3de8-31a0-25ef-456d","priority":3,"repos":["rebar"],"tags":["comments","documentation","maintainability","grouped-remediation"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Condense comments in scripts — cohort 03: check_import_walk–jira_dc_capability_map"},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788570606678522467,"uuid":"ed892993-f29f-4831-83f8-4254b6df326e"}